            ("What region forms at the metallurgical junction of P-type and N-type silicon where free electrons and holes diffuse and recombine?", "Depletion Region (Space Charge Region)", ["Conduction Channel", "Inversion Layer", "Ohmic Contact"], "Mobile carriers diffuse across the junction, leaving uncompensated ionized donor (+) and acceptor (-) dopant atoms that form an electric field."),
            ("What is the built-in barrier potential across the depletion region of a standard silicon P-N junction diode at room temperature?", "Approximately 0.6 to 0.7 Volts", ["0.2 to 0.3 Volts", "1.5 to 2.0 Volts", "0.0 Volts"], "Forward bias must overcome this internal 0.7V electrostatic barrier before significant diffusion current flows."),
            ("What bias condition is applied to a P-N junction diode when the positive terminal of a voltage source connects to the anode?", "Forward Bias", ["Reverse Bias", "Zero Bias", "Breakdown Bias"], "Forward bias opposes the internal built-in electric field, narrowing the depletion region and allowing exponential current."),
