            ("What reverse breakdown mechanism occurs in heavily doped P-N junctions at low reverse voltages under 5V via quantum mechanical tunneling?", "Zener Breakdown", ["Avalanche Breakdown", "Thermal Breakdown", "Dielectric Puncture"], "Narrow depletion barriers in heavily doped junctions allow valence electrons to tunnel directly into the conduction band under high electric fields."),
            ("What reverse breakdown mechanism occurs in lightly doped junctions at higher reverse voltages above 6V via carrier impact ionization?", "Avalanche Breakdown", ["Zener Breakdown", "Tunneling Breakdown", "Electroluminescent Breakdown"], "Thermally accelerated electrons gain kinetic energy in the depletion field, knocking valence electrons loose in a cascading avalanche."),
