            ("What parameter defines the small DC current that flows through a reverse-biased diode prior to reaching breakdown?", "Reverse Saturation Current (Is)", ["Forward Knee Current", "Holding Current", "Peak Inverse Current"], "Reverse leakage current is governed by thermal generation of minority carriers in the depletion layer, doubling roughly every 10 C."),
            ("What does the Peak Inverse Voltage (PIV) rating of a semiconductor rectifier diode signify?", "The maximum instantaneous reverse voltage that the diode can withstand without breaking down", ["The forward threshold voltage", "The voltage at peak forward current", "The continuous RMS working voltage"], "Exceeding a diode's PIV rating causes uncontrolled reverse breakdown and catastrophic thermal destruction."),
            ("What wide-bandgap semiconductor material with a bandgap around 3.2 eV is replacing silicon in high-voltage electric vehicle inverters?", "Silicon Carbide (SiC)", ["Gallium Arsenide (GaAs)", "Germanium (Ge)", "Indium Phosphide (InP)"], "SiC offers 10x higher breakdown electric field strength and superior thermal conductivity, slashing switching losses in EV inverters."),
            ("What high-electron-mobility wide-bandgap semiconductor with a bandgap around 3.4 eV dominates high-frequency RF power amplifiers and compact fast chargers?", "Gallium Nitride (GaN)", ["Silicon Carbide", "Silicon", "Germanium"], "GaN transistors achieve high electron saturation velocity and low on-resistance, enabling compact, high-efficiency power converters."),
            ("What term describes the ratio of collector current to base current in a Bipolar Junction Transistor common-emitter configuration?", "DC Current Gain (Beta or hFE)", ["Alpha", "Transconductance (gm)", "Amplification Factor"], "Beta (hFE) typically ranges from 50 to 300 in small-signal BJTs, defining how much small base current controls collector output current."),
            ("What operational state of a BJT occurs when both the base-emitter and base-collector junctions are forward-biased?", "Saturation Region", ["Cutoff Region", "Active (Linear) Region", "Breakdown Region"], "In saturation, collector-emitter voltage drops to its minimum (VCE(sat) ~0.1 to 0.2V), conducting maximum collector load current."),
            ("What operational state of a BJT occurs when the base-emitter junction is reverse-biased, resulting in virtually zero collector current?", "Cutoff Region", ["Saturation Region", "Active Region", "Ohmic Region"], "In cutoff, collector current is virtually zero, acting like an open mechanical switch contact."),
            ("In what BJT operating region is the base-emitter junction forward-biased and the base-collector junction reverse-biased?", "Active (Linear) Region", ["Saturation Region", "Cutoff Region", "Inverted Region"], "In the active region, small changes in base current produce proportional linear changes in collector current."),
            ("What fundamental equation relates BJT collector current to base-emitter voltage?", "Ebers-Moll Equation", ["Ohm's Law", "Einstein Relation", "Poisson Equation"], "The exponential relationship demonstrates that a tiny increase in VBE produces a massive exponential surge in collector current."),
