            ("What high-frequency effect describes the unwanted capacitive multiplication between the input and output terminals of an inverting amplifier?", "Miller Effect", ["Early Effect", "Barkhausen Criterion", "Skin Effect"], "The Miller effect multiplies feedback capacitance by amplifier voltage gain, restricting high-frequency bandwidth."),
            ("What logic circuit technology pairs N-channel and P-channel MOSFETs to achieve virtually zero static power consumption?", "CMOS (Complementary Metal-Oxide-Semiconductor)", ["TTL", "ECL", "NMOS Logic"], "In CMOS gates, one transistor is always off when the other is on, drawing current only dynamically during switching transitions."),
