            ("What type of memory in a modern microcontroller retains program code non-volatiles when power is removed and can be electrically erased in blocks?", "Flash Memory", ["SRAM", "DRAM", "Mask ROM"], "Flash memory stores the executable firmware, surviving power cycles and supporting in-system reprogramming."),
